diff --git a/docs/privacy-audits.md b/docs/privacy-audits.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bcd0199
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/privacy-audits.md
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Privacy and service review register
+
+No independent audit has been completed or supplied. Dependency scanning is an automated check, not an independent assurance report. Integrations that collect user data remain disabled until their review is complete.
+
+| Service | Data previously shared | Current status | Evidence required before enabling |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Demo Cloud Functions accounts | Username and password | Removed; account forms unavailable | Provider identity, security assessment, authentication design, deletion API, retention and subprocessor terms |
+| Cloud Functions analytics / advertising | Browser activity and network metadata | Scripts and ad registration removed | Defined purpose, minimal event schema, consent controls, independent audit and retention evidence |
+| Google Fonts | IP address and request metadata | Removed; system fonts | Necessity and privacy review if reintroduced |
+| Imgur / CinemAI images | IP address and request metadata | Replaced with existing local editorial photos | Necessity and vendor review if reintroduced |
+| Hosting / TLS termination | IP addresses, URLs, operational logs | Required infrastructure; review outstanding | Access control, log redaction, retention, regional hosting, encryption, incident process and audit evidence |
+
+## Required review process
+
+The operator owns the register. Before adding a service, record its owner, purpose, fields transmitted, legal basis where applicable, hosting region, subprocessors, retention, deletion mechanism, access controls, encryption in transit and at rest, and incident contact. Collect an independent assessment (for example, a relevant SOC 2 report or scoped penetration test), inspect its scope, date, exceptions and remediation, and link the actual evidence in an access-controlled register. Record approval and next review date; review at least annually and after material changes or incidents. An expired or unresolved review blocks enabling the integration.
+
+An account integration additionally needs a first-party server endpoint, an explicitly allowlisted HTTPS destination, request size limits, timeouts, generic public errors, rate limiting, and secure server-managed authentication. Do not restore browser requests to the demo endpoint. Do not store passwords or bearer tokens in client storage. New optional analytics must remain off until explicitly enabled by the visitor, with withdrawal controls and sensitive forms excluded.
+
+## Independent application audit
+
+Commission an independent auditor before enabling account processing, and repeat at least annually and after significant security changes. Scope includes data flows, CSP and CSRF behavior, session isolation and expiry, dependency risks, hosting log retention, backup deletion, secrets, authorization and incident handling. Supply a data inventory, architecture, test results and service register. Track findings by severity, owner and due date; resolve critical and high findings before release. Record the auditor, date, scope, evidence link, remediation and next review date here. All fields are currently pending; do not display an audit badge or claim certification.
+
+## Application retention and deployment
+
+Diagnostic article scripts, including oversized cookie writes and unnecessary statistics requests, have been removed. Only article IDs and a random session ID are retained. Reading-list entries expire after 24 hours from the last write; timers physically remove abandoned entries. Deleting the list or removing its last item destroys the session. At most 100 IDs per list and 10,000 sessions are retained. Storage is process-local memory and is discarded on restart; multiple instances do not share reading lists. Under load, oldest lists may expire early. A distributed deployment must use a reviewed private session store with enforced TTL and deletion before promising durable lists.
+
+Production requires HTTPS, an HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Strict cookie, and trusted proxy configuration. Ensure the edge delivers HSTS and these security headers on static assets and infrastructure error responses as well; application middleware covers routed pages and APIs. Do not trust client-supplied forwarding headers. Never log request bodies, authorization headers, cookies or reading lists. The hosting operator must separately configure minimal log fields, access, short retention, regional processing and deletion; application controls cannot purge provider logs.
+
+## Automated evidence
+
+Run `pnpm build`, `pnpm test`, and `pnpm audit:dependencies`. CI runs all three on pull requests and weekly. Tests launch the production server without a browser and cover cookieless browsing, security headers, blocked cross-site mutations, validation, bounded request bodies, session isolation, export, deletion, cookie flags and storage expiry. Dependency findings must be assessed and fixed before merging; retain CI results as review evidence. This does not replace a human or independent audit.
+
+Astro's production CSP header includes hashes for inline scripts; middleware preserves that policy and adds frame restrictions. Astro may reject cross-origin requests before application middleware runs; edge headers must also cover those early rejections. Script execution and connections are restricted to this origin. Inline styles are permitted for React and the transition router. Framework reference: https://docs.astro.build/en/reference/configuration-reference/#securitycsp
